From: Robert DeLanghe <1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:43:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] test(examples): the examples a producer can make are made by
 one

step-01-minimal and path-01-pr are path p track's output byte for byte
(track init gains --id and --base-branch so the output is reproducible);
path-02-local-session is the document path p derive claude makes from the
real recorded session test-fixtures/claude/convo.jsonl; graph-01-release is
path p merge over the real Codex, Gemini CLI and Pi sessions; the JSONL
twins come from the streaming writer. examples_generated.rs fails on drift
(scripts/gen-examples.sh regenerates). The rest stay illustrative, listed
in examples/README.md with a qualifier concern each: no producer emits
structural AST ops, signatures, merge steps or step fragments. Quotes and
tests that leaned on the hand-written content follow. pr/54.
